  "body": "Expose ISO 10303-44 STEP assembly paths and instance names in `camcraft-kernel` so multi-part vendor STEP files can map subassemblies to `.mch` parts.\n\n## Context\n`crates/kernel/src/solidcore_step.rs` returns a flat `Vec<StepSolid>` where each solid holds only `item: u64` and `name: String`, and `crates/geometry/src/step.rs` merges all solids into one `Mesh`. Multi-part vendor machine STEP assemblies cannot map named subassemblies (base, saddle, table, head) to `.mch` part IDs without manual CAD splitting first.\n\n## Scope\n- Read ISO 10303-44 product assembly structure (`NEXT_ASSEMBLY_USAGE_OCCURRENCE` and parent product names) in `camcraft-kernel` alongside `StepSolid` and `StepSheet`.\n- Return each solid's assembly path (parent-to-leaf product and instance names) in millimetres without changing the existing `StepSolid` geometry or validation checks.\n- Expose solid-to-assembly-path metadata through `camcraft-geometry::step` so callers can filter or partition solids by subassembly name.\n- Keep existing `import_step` and `import_step_model` callers and error messages unchanged.\n\n## Done means\nTests on a multi-part STEP assembly fixture return each solid's assembly path and instance name in millimetres, handle unnamed occurrences without panic, and pass all existing `camcraft-kernel` and `camcraft-geometry` STEP tests.\n\nPart of #3239\n",
